  "steppingRootCause": "The Forward control loses its title attribute after being clicked: TradingView's apply-common-tooltip machinery strips `title` while its own tooltip is up and does not restore it while the pointer stays on the button. Measured by diffing the toolbar around one click - same position, same classes, title=\"Forward\" becomes title=\"\". A [title=\"Forward\"] locator is therefore single-use, which is why every multi-step run reported that the frame never advanced. Resolving the control structurally (controls__button index 1, after Play) fixed it: 18 successful steps in this run against 1 before.",
  "disprovenHypotheses": [
    "the control scrolls out of view - refuted: the toolbar does not overflow (scrollWidth == clientWidth) and scrollIntoViewIfNeeded cannot rescue it",
    "reading the Data Window between steps breaks it - refuted: it vanishes with no reads at all",
    "Bar Replay exits - refuted: isBarReplayActive stays true, the toolbar stays, the header toggle is unchanged",
    "5m survives more steps than 15m - refuted: identical, one step each; the earlier '3 steps' were three CASES with one step each"
  ],
  "htf4hOpenQuestion": "HTF-4H reports 2025-10-27T17:30:00Z -> 2025-10-27T20:00:00Z, 150 minutes, and the checker calls that not-a-whole-frame. The US regular session is 6.5h (13:30-20:00 UTC), so a 4h grid does not fit it: the first bar spans 13:30-17:30 and the second is TRUNCATED at the session close to 2.5h. The violation is therefore most likely a false positive of the checker, the fourth assumption of this kind found today. It is deliberately NOT loosened without an owner decision - three such rules have already been relaxed on evidence (absolute UTC grid, interval display label, market gaps) and a fourth needs to be a conscious choice, not a reflex.",
  "failClosedNote": "The 15m observation returned no diagnostics at all in this run (previous run: available=0, PASS). That is the fail-closed path working - an empty Data Window read cannot pass - but it makes the case flaky at that step and it is reported as such."
